          "name": "OpenAI SDK",
          "content": "\n\n\n\nFor additional information, see [the OpenAI .NET API library](https://github.com/openai/openai-dotnet).\n\n\n## 1. Create a personal access token\n\n\nYou'll need to **[create a token](https://github.com/settings/tokens?type=beta)** to enable free API access.\n\nYou **do not need to give any permissions** to the token. Note that the token will be sent to a Microsoft service.\n\nTo use the code snippets below, create an environment variable to set your token as the key for the client code.\n\nIf you're using **bash**:\n\n```bash\nexport GITHUB_TOKEN=\"<your-github-token-goes-here>\"\n```\n\nIf you're in **powershell**:\n\n```powershell\n$Env:GITHUB_TOKEN=\"<your-github-token-goes-here>\"\n```\n\nIf you're using Windows command prompt:\n\n```\nset GITHUB_TOKEN=<your-github-token-goes-here>\n```\n\n\n\n## 2. Install dependencies\n\n1. Install [dotnet runtime](https://dotnet.microsoft.com/en-us/download/dotnet/)\n2. Open power shell at the desired project folder, restore the environment and run the program.\n\n```\ndotnet restore\ndotnet run\n```\n\n\n\n## 3. Run a basic code sample\n\nThis sample demonstrates a call to embeddings API. It is leveraging the GitHub AI model inference endpoint and your GitHub token. The call is synchronous.\n\n```csharp\nusing OpenAI;\nusing OpenAI.Embeddings;\nusing System.Text.Json;\n\nvar endpoint = new Uri(\"https://models.inference.ai.azure.com\");\nvar credential = System.Environment.GetEnvironmentVariable(\"GITHUB_TOKEN\");\nvar model = \"text-embedding-3-large\";\n\nvar openAIOptions = new OpenAIClientOptions()\n{\n    Endpoint=endpoint\n};\n\nvar client = new EmbeddingClient(model, credential, openAIOptions);\n\nEmbeddingCollection response = client.GenerateEmbeddings(\n    new List<string>{\n        \"first phrase\", \"second phrase\", \"third phrase\"\n    }\n);\n\nforeach (Embedding embedding in response){\n    ReadOnlyMemory<float> vector = embedding.Vector;\n    int length = vector.Length;\n    System.Console.Write($\"data[{embedding.Index}]: length={length}, \");\n    System.Console.Write($\"[{vector.Span[0]}, {vector.Span[1]}, ..., \");\n    System.Console.WriteLine($\"{vector.Span[length - 2]}, {vector.Span[length - 1]}]\");\n}\n```\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n## 4. Going beyond rate limits\n\nThe rate limits for the playground and free API usage are intended to help you experiment with models and prototype your AI application. For use beyond those limits, and to bring your application to scale, you must provision resources from an Azure account, and authenticate from there instead of your GitHub personal access token. You don't need to change anything else in your code. Use this link to [discover how to go beyond the free tier limits in Azure AI](https://ai.azure.com/github?modelName=text-embedding-3-large).",
